      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm glad you could make it in today. What brings you in to see me?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S021",
      "patient_response": "Hi, thank you so much for seeing me. I really appreciate you taking the time. \n\nUm, I guess I came in because... well, it's probably nothing too serious, just a little communication hiccup, really. I'm an artist, and lately I've been getting some feedback that my artist statements and my client notes are a little... hard to follow? \n\nPeople keep telling me they don't really understand what I'm trying to explain. Like, in meetings, I guess I start jumping around a lot. I'll go from talking about, you know, the physical textures of a piece, straight into the budgets, and then... well, sometimes I get really into the, um, the secret meanings behind the work. Which I guess throws people off. \n\nI'm probably just being a little too scattered, right? I just really don't want to make a bad impression on my clients or seem unprofessional, so I thought it would be best to come talk to someone. Is that an okay reason to be here? I hope I'm explaining this right.",
