    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever had experiences where you heard sounds or voices that other people couldn't hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Um... well... I guess, maybe a little bit? But it's really nothing major, I promise. It's probably just because I spend so much time alone in the studio, you know? When it's really quiet, your mind can sort of play tricks on you.\n\nSometimes, when I'm working by myself, I'll hear... like, a woman's voice? Just very quietly commenting on things, coming from behind the supply shelves. Or, um, occasionally I'll get this really strong smell of hot metal near a piece I haven't finished yet. \n\nAnd in the moment, it feels completely, one hundred percent real. But then I'll go check behind the shelves, or look for a short circuit, and... there's absolutely nothing there. \n\nIt's just stress and being tired, right? Like, sensory overload from focusing too hard? I really try not to let it bother me, and I definitely don't let it interfere with my deadlines. I hope that doesn't make me sound too crazy... is that something that happens to people when they're just overworked?",
